    "dibia": {
      "beats": [
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "On the way home you pass the stream path. Dibia Ọ̀kwụ̀ is sitting outside his shrine, peeling an orange with a knife older than the village."
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "dibia",
          "text": "Nwa Nwankwo. Come. I see white cloth on your road. A white book that writes in red. A room where everybody smiles and nobody laughs."
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "speaker": "dibia",
          "text": "\"Will you listen to an old man?\"",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "\"What does it mean?\"",
              "effects": {
                "remember": {
                  "dibia": "listened"
                },
                "changeStat": {
                  "conscience": 3
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "\"Old man, your eyes are tired.\"",
              "effects": {
                "remember": {
                  "dibia": "mocked"
                },
                "changeStat": {
                  "conscience": -2
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "Give him ₦1,000 for a blessing.",
              "effects": {
                "setFlag": "dibiaCharm",
                "remember": {
                  "dibia": "paid"
                }
              },
              "cost": 1000
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "dibia",
          "text": "When they ask what you love, lie. When they ask what you fear, tell the truth. When they offer you a white cloth, remember the name of your mother.",
          "if": {
            "memory": {
              "dibia": "listened"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "dibia",
          "text": "(He ties a small red thread on your wrist.) Keep it. Thread is cheap. What it remembers is not.",
          "if": "dibiaCharm"
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "dibia",
          "text": "(He laughs. It's a kind laugh, which is worse.) Go, then. The road will teach you what I couldn't.",
          "if": {
            "memory": {
              "dibia": "mocked"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "goto",
          "scene": "farewell"
        }
      ],
      "location": "shrine",
      "time": "dusk"
    },
    "farewell": {
      "beats": [
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Nkwọ day. 9 p.m. The Lagos bus coughs at the junction like an old man about to give a speech."
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "nneEmeka",
          "text": "My son. (She presses a folded ₦5,000 into your palm.) It's the last of the palm-oil money. Take it. Lagos is not kind to empty pockets."
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "speaker": "nneEmeka",
          "text": "(Her hand is shaking.)",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "Take it. You'll need it.",
              "effects": {
                "changeStat": {
                  "money": 5000,
                  "motherBond": -3
                },
                "setFlag": "tookNneMoney"
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "Close her hand around it. \"Keep it, Nne. I'll send more than this.\"",
              "effects": {
                "changeStat": {
                  "motherBond": 6,
                  "conscience": 3
                },
                "remember": {
                  "nneMoney": "refused"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "She doesn't know about the land. When she finds out, she will remember this night. So will you.",
          "if": "soldLand"
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "Behind the bus, the big tree. Under it, an empty box. Somebody will open it tomorrow.",
          "if": "tookHarvest"
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "chinwe",
          "text": "So. Lagos. (She's holding her wrapper very tightly.) What should I do while you're gone?",
          "if": {
            "notFlags": [
              "chinweGone"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "choice",
          "speaker": "chinwe",
          "text": "\"Tell me the truth.\"",
          "options": [
            {
              "text": "\"Wait for me. I will send for you.\"",
              "effects": {
                "remember": {
                  "chinwePromise": "sendFor"
                },
                "changeStat": {
                  "chinweBond": 5
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "\"Wait one year. If I don't come back, marry another man.\"",
              "effects": {
                "remember": {
                  "chinwePromise": "oneYear"
                },
                "changeStat": {
                  "chinweBond": 2
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text": "\"Don't wait for me, Chinwe.\"",
              "effects": {
                "remember": {
                  "chinwePromise": "dontWait"
                },
                "changeStat": {
                  "chinweBond": -10,
                  "conscience": 4
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "dialogue",
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "text": "You have {money}. Not ₦150,000. Ike will see it in your face before you open your mouth.",
          "if": "shortOfFee"
        },
